      "body": "I can take this up; please assign me if the direction is accepted. An efficient implementation would reuse the wallet label/metadata path, map only the BIP-329 record types Core can represent, and add round-trip tests for supported, malformed, and unsupported records while preserving the existing wallet behavior. The less-obvious factor is that labels can contain sensitive personal context: import should avoid partial wallet changes on invalid input, and export must not leak the payload through logs or an unexpected output path. I would make those failure and output semantics explicit before adding the interface.",
